{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/98485-is-the-wod-core-book-really-needed-to-play-demon-the-descent","id":98485,"title":"Is the WoD core book really needed to play Demon:The Descent?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-25T11:11:35-07:00","id":98485,"title":"Is the WoD core book really needed to play Demon:The Descent?","content":"I'm sure this has been answered before, but I don't frequent these forums, and my searches didn't turn up the answer. I know Blood and Smoke is a complete game, supposedly it has everything you need to play, including the new God-Machine rules baked in. Is Demon: The Descent organized the same way? Can I run a game just out of just the one book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T11:19:30-07:00","id":98491,"title":"","content":"<i>Descent</i> DOES require the WoD corebook. Admittedly, the GMC-update appendix has so much stuff in it that almost the only thing you get from the corebook is how the dice work and what the Attributes/Skills are. But it's still technically necessary for a new player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1812-deflare","name":"Deflare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T11:25:29-07:00","id":98498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deflare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/98485-is-the-wod-core-book-really-needed-to-play-demon-the-descent?p=98491#post98491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Descent</i> DOES require the WoD corebook. Admittedly, the GMC-update appendix has so much stuff in it that almost the only thing you get from the corebook is how the dice work and what the Attributes/Skills are. But it's still technically necessary for a new player.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I have the core book, I was just hoping I wouldn't have to go back and forth. Is there a reason why Blood and Smoke has a full rule set but Demon doesn't? I assumed the all-in-one format was what they were going to run with after Blood and Smoke came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T11:30:54-07:00","id":98505,"title":"","content":"I'm going to say that no, it doesn't really need it. Looks to me like everything is there in the Demon core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T11:44:48-07:00","id":98514,"title":"","content":"Most of what you need from the core book is the skill descriptions, specialties, attributes. And the basic rules that weren't changed in the god machine chronicle update. The god machine chronicle update is actually part of the Demon book, so you don't need that. I would guess that it doesn't contain the corebook stuff because of its size, Demon is already 400 pages while Blood &amp; Smoke is only 300.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1105-hulsmanm","name":"hulsmanm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T11:53:26-07:00","id":98529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/98485-is-the-wod-core-book-really-needed-to-play-demon-the-descent?p=98498#post98498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, I have the core book, I was just hoping I wouldn't have to go back and forth. Is there a reason why Blood and Smoke has a full rule set but Demon doesn't? I assumed the all-in-one format was what they were going to run with after Blood and Smoke came out.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'd have to guess, the reasoning goes this way:<br /> <br /> Demon is currently about 100 pages longer than B&amp;S.<br /> Demon needs the ephemeral being rules and B&amp;S did not.<br /> If they added the Attribute and Skill descriptions, then that would add about 10 more pages to the book (going by the B&amp;S PDF). <br /> Adding those pages would push the standard PoD over the $50 mark. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T14:25:04-07:00","id":98655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/98485-is-the-wod-core-book-really-needed-to-play-demon-the-descent#post98485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure this has been answered before, but I don't frequent these forums, and my searches didn't turn up the answer. I know Blood and Smoke is a complete game, supposedly it has everything you need to play, including the new God-Machine rules baked in. Is Demon: The Descent organized the same way? Can I run a game just out of just the one book?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you've got <i>Blood and Smoke</i>, you don't need the nWoD core to run <i>Demon</i>. The <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/rules-of-the-night/\" target=\"_blank\">draft of the core rules chapter from B&amp;S</a> is also available on the blog, and would work for <i>Demon</i>. There were hardly any mechanical changes between that draft and the one in the book; most of the differences are clarifications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T15:50:00-07:00","id":98725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/98485-is-the-wod-core-book-really-needed-to-play-demon-the-descent?p=98655#post98655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you've got <i>Blood and Smoke</i>, you don't need the nWoD core to run <i>Demon</i>. The <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/rules-of-the-night/\" target=\"_blank\">draft of the core rules chapter from B&amp;S</a> is also available on the blog, and would work for <i>Demon</i>. There were hardly any mechanical changes between that draft and the one in the book; most of the differences are clarifications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's perfect! As long as i can find all the base mechanics answers in one book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}